WEBVTT

00:00.620 --> 00:03.510
Zane is a dangerous
fellow who likes

00:03.510 --> 00:08.180
to go rock climbing
inside an active volcano.

00:08.180 --> 00:10.000
He is a dangerous fellow.

00:10.000 --> 00:12.070
He just heard some
rumblings, so he's

00:12.070 --> 00:15.030
decided to climb out
as quickly as he can.

00:15.030 --> 00:17.890
Zane's elevation
relative to the edge

00:17.890 --> 00:20.630
of the inside of the
volcano in meters,

00:20.630 --> 00:24.560
E, as a function of time in
seconds is shown in the table

00:24.560 --> 00:25.410
below.

00:25.410 --> 00:27.140
Zane climbs at a constant rate.

00:27.140 --> 00:29.850
So this guy, I mean if we
were to draw a volcano here,

00:29.850 --> 00:32.210
this guy is just kind of silly.

00:32.210 --> 00:35.790
So this is my volcano.

00:35.790 --> 00:40.280
And he's actually
climbing on the inside

00:40.280 --> 00:41.680
of an active volcano.

00:41.680 --> 00:45.310
So there's probably smoke and
ash and all the other stuff

00:45.310 --> 00:46.870
coming out of this thing.

00:46.870 --> 00:50.240
So this really is
dangerous for him.

00:50.240 --> 00:53.320
And let's say that this
right over here is Zane.

00:53.320 --> 01:00.230
He's climbing up from
inside the active volcano.

01:00.230 --> 01:02.610
So let's think about
what they're telling us.

01:02.610 --> 01:05.069
So based on the table, which
of these statements is true?

01:05.069 --> 01:07.360
So I'm not going to even look
at these statements here.

01:07.360 --> 01:11.210
I'm just going to try
to interpret this.

01:11.210 --> 01:16.510
So his elevation as a
function of time in seconds

01:16.510 --> 01:18.240
is shown in the table below.

01:18.240 --> 01:21.930
So his elevation is negative
24 when time is equal to 0.

01:21.930 --> 01:24.230
And this table is done in a
kind of nontraditional way.

01:24.230 --> 01:26.640
Normally, we would
have the input

01:26.640 --> 01:29.270
into the function on
the left-hand side.

01:29.270 --> 01:32.172
And then we would have
the function of it

01:32.172 --> 01:33.130
on the right-hand side.

01:33.130 --> 01:34.690
And actually I like
looking at things that way,

01:34.690 --> 01:36.240
so I'm going to
make it like that.

01:36.240 --> 01:41.120
So let me copy and paste this so
I can put it on the other side.

01:41.120 --> 01:46.090
So let me cut and let me paste
it, paste it right over here.

01:46.090 --> 01:49.190
So this one, now I can think
of it a little bit clearer.

01:49.190 --> 01:53.750
So at time 0, he's going to
be at negative 24 meters.

01:53.750 --> 01:56.770
At time 4 seconds, he's going
to be at negative 21 meters.

01:56.770 --> 02:01.800
So this makes a little bit
clearer, at least in my head.

02:01.800 --> 02:04.060
So let's think about
what's happening.

02:04.060 --> 02:05.060
So where does he start?

02:05.060 --> 02:07.000
At time equals 0, where is he?

02:07.000 --> 02:09.501
Well at time equals
0, he is 24 meters

02:09.501 --> 02:10.750
below the edge of the volcano.

02:10.750 --> 02:13.200
So this distance
at time equals 0,

02:13.200 --> 02:16.235
this distance right
over here is 24 meters.

02:16.235 --> 02:17.860
And we could even
plot this in a graph.

02:21.710 --> 02:25.470
So this is his elevation
relative to the edge,

02:25.470 --> 02:27.070
and it is a function of time.

02:27.070 --> 02:28.420
I'll write it like that.

02:28.420 --> 02:30.700
And it is negative
most of this time.

02:30.700 --> 02:35.160
So I'm going to make the
t-axis a little bit higher.

02:35.160 --> 02:38.350
So it looks something like that.

02:38.350 --> 02:39.880
That's our t-axis.

02:39.880 --> 02:42.630
And when t is equal to 0,
we see that his elevation

02:42.630 --> 02:44.660
is negative 24 meters.

02:44.660 --> 02:49.310
So his elevation is
negative 24 meters.

02:49.310 --> 02:53.720
So he's going to, this is
right here at 0 seconds.

02:53.720 --> 02:58.080
And then when time increases
by 4, so our change in time

02:58.080 --> 03:01.235
is equal to 4, what's
his change in elevation?

03:01.235 --> 03:04.210
Well, his change in
elevation is, let's see,

03:04.210 --> 03:07.610
he's going from negative
24 to negative 21.

03:07.610 --> 03:08.970
He increased by 3.

03:08.970 --> 03:13.690
So his change in elevation
is equal to positive 3.

03:13.690 --> 03:15.580
He increased by 3.

03:15.580 --> 03:18.240
So at what rate is he increasing
his elevation with respect

03:18.240 --> 03:19.130
to time?

03:19.130 --> 03:24.130
Well, change in elevation
is equal to 3 per unit.

03:24.130 --> 03:28.470
And that's 3 when
his change in time.

03:28.470 --> 03:32.900
And remember this triangle just
means a Greek letter delta,

03:32.900 --> 03:34.340
shorthand for change in.

03:34.340 --> 03:38.686
So change in elevation over
change in times is 3 over 4.

03:38.686 --> 03:40.060
So one way to
think about this is

03:40.060 --> 03:43.575
that he goes 3/4 of
a meter per second.

03:46.800 --> 03:47.970
The units up here is meter.

03:47.970 --> 03:49.890
The units down here is second.

03:49.890 --> 03:51.940
So he goes 3/4 of
a meter per second.

03:51.940 --> 03:53.410
And we can verify that.

03:53.410 --> 03:58.840
The next row here, we see
our change in time is 8.

04:01.460 --> 04:03.116
So it's twice as
much time has passed,

04:03.116 --> 04:04.990
so he should have gone
twice as much distance

04:04.990 --> 04:05.990
if his rate is constant.

04:05.990 --> 04:07.920
Let's verify that
that's the case.

04:07.920 --> 04:10.980
So he went from negative
21 to negative 15.

04:10.980 --> 04:14.460
His elevation increased by 6.

04:14.460 --> 04:16.399
So change in elevation
over change in time

04:16.399 --> 04:18.640
is 6/8, which is the
same thing as 3/4.

04:18.640 --> 04:21.200
So you see that he has
this constant change.

04:21.200 --> 04:22.950
So let's plot a few
of these points.

04:22.950 --> 04:27.360
So when time is 0, his
elevation is negative 24.

04:27.360 --> 04:32.240
When time is 4,
right over there,

04:32.240 --> 04:34.410
his elevation is negative 21.

04:34.410 --> 04:38.110
Let's say this looks
something like this.

04:38.110 --> 04:42.040
And so his elevation
as a function of time

04:42.040 --> 04:43.635
is going to look
something like this.

04:46.240 --> 04:49.140
Let me actually draw it a
little bit more to scale.

04:49.140 --> 04:52.520
Because the other
thing that we do know

04:52.520 --> 04:55.420
is that when time is
32, his elevation is 0.

04:55.420 --> 04:56.920
So let me put that
right over there.

04:56.920 --> 04:59.890
When time is 32,
his elevation is 0.

04:59.890 --> 05:02.580
So his elevation as
a function of time

05:02.580 --> 05:03.795
looks something like this.

05:07.030 --> 05:10.480
And we could plot other
points there when time is 4.

05:10.480 --> 05:12.360
So 4 is going to
be at this half.

05:12.360 --> 05:12.880
That's a 4.

05:12.880 --> 05:15.080
So 4 is going to be
right over there.

05:15.080 --> 05:18.410
His elevation is negative 21.

05:18.410 --> 05:20.250
So this is a general idea.

05:20.250 --> 05:22.510
He starts at negative
24 meters and he

05:22.510 --> 05:25.160
increases at a rate of
3/4 meters per second.

05:25.160 --> 05:27.980
So which of these
choices is correct?

05:27.980 --> 05:30.970
Zane was 24 meters below
the edge of the volcano when

05:30.970 --> 05:34.160
he decided to leave,
and he climbs 3 meters

05:34.160 --> 05:36.350
every 4 seconds on the way out.

05:36.350 --> 05:37.180
That seems right.

05:37.180 --> 05:39.092
He climbs 3 meters
every 4 seconds.

05:39.092 --> 05:40.550
So we're going to
go with that one.

05:40.550 --> 05:42.270
Let's make sure that
these aren't right.

05:42.270 --> 05:44.204
Zane was 24 meters
below the volcano when

05:44.204 --> 05:45.620
he decided to
leave, and he climbs

05:45.620 --> 05:47.210
4 meters every 3 seconds.

05:47.210 --> 05:49.190
No, no, it's 3 meters
every 4 seconds.

05:49.190 --> 05:50.640
So that's not right.

05:50.640 --> 05:53.060
Zane was 32 meters below
the edge of the volcano.

05:53.060 --> 05:54.420
No, that's not right.

05:54.420 --> 05:55.620
Zane was 32 meters.

05:55.620 --> 05:57.950
That's not right either.
